  production binding to the KMP charge-planner repositories (useRatePlans / useChargePlans
  / useOptimizeCharge / useApplySchedule) attaches at that seam (ADR-004), exactly as every
  other P4 surface defers its live wiring. The navigation registration injects an in-memory
  source seeded with the static rate-plan fallback + an empty resolved history so the page
  renders its real pre-data state (no placeholder screen, ADR-011).
• Charts/maps: none required by the manifest. The 24-hour rate timeline is a native SwiftUI
  bar visualization (NOT a chart library, NOT a WKWebView) with pointer tooltips (.help) +
  VoiceOver labels.
• Units: the charge-planner DTO predates SI canonicalization and is rendered at web parity
  (currency, ¢/kWh, kWh, %, h) via the shared TSCurrency/TSFormattedNumber formatters; no
  non-SI value is stored or computed.
• Tests: per-surface XCTest belongs in the `Tests/Unit/` TEST target (which links XCTest +
